#!/usr/bin/env perl
# PODNAME: holmgang
# ABSTRACT: Lint Holmgang suites, run them against a Langertha engine, evaluate the reports

our $VERSION = '0.001';

use strict;
use warnings;
use Langertha::Holmgang::CLI;

binmode STDOUT, ':encoding(UTF-8)';
binmode STDERR, ':encoding(UTF-8)';

exit Langertha::Holmgang::CLI->new->run(@ARGV);

=synopsis

  holmgang lint /srv/suites/demo-fan /srv/more-suites

  LANGERTHA_OPENAI_API_KEY=... holmgang run --suite /srv/suites/demo-fan \
    --target OpenAI --model gpt-4o-mini --repeat 3 --report /data/reports/run.json

  holmgang run --suite /srv/suites/demo-fan --target vLLM \
    --url http://10.0.0.5:8000/v1 --model some-model \
    --variant max_tokens=4000 --variant enable_thinking=off --concurrency 4

  # two variants of one target, side by side in the report
  holmgang run --suite /srv/suites/demo-fan --target vLLM --url http://10.0.0.5:8000/v1 \
    --variant think-off:enable_thinking=off \
    --variant think-on:enable_thinking=on --variant think-on:deadline=1800 \
    --report /data/reports/run.json

  # continue a run that was cut off: only the missing results are played
  holmgang run ... --resume /data/reports/run.json --report /data/reports/run.json

  holmgang run --suite /srv/suites/demo-fan --target mock-solution   # dry run, no network

  holmgang report /data/reports/*.json --by topic --format markdown --suite /srv/suites/demo-fan

=description

The command line of L<Langertha::Holmgang> (ADR 0009). Three commands:

B<lint> loads each suite exactly as a run would -- format 2 shape checks, lint
and its two mock runs -- and prints C<ok> with every case, or C<FAIL> with the
refusal, which names the case file and the field. An argument is a suite
directory (it holds F<suite.yaml>) or a directory of suites.

B<run> plays every case of the suites against one target, under each of its
variants, repetition after repetition, with at most C<--concurrency> requests
open at once (L<Langertha::Holmgang::Batch>); it prints one line per case and
repetition as each ends and then the evaluation per topic. With C<--report> it
writes the JSON report (ADR 0006), also while the run goes on, so a run that
is cut off can be continued with C<--resume>. Write reports outside any
checkout: a report quotes its cases. SIGINT or SIGTERM cancels: no further
case starts, the cases in play finish, the report is written (the run
C<cancelled>); a second signal ends the process at once.

B<report> reads report files, joins them, and prints the evaluation per topic:
the comparison of targets, the verdicts per suite and, where cases have a
length tier, the tier curves.

B<Exit codes:> C<0> everything loaded or ran and every verdict is ok; C<1> a
suite was refused (lint), a verdict is not ok (run, report), or the target
answered no case of the run -- every result C<error>, C<context_exceeded> or
C<no_vision> (run; said on standard error with the count per status and the
first error text, the report is written all the same); C<2> a usage or setup
error, or a run that aborted or was cancelled.

B<Keys:> holmgang reads no key. An engine takes its key from where Langertha
reads it, its environment variable (C<LANGERTHA_OPENAI_API_KEY>,
C<LANGERTHA_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY> ...). There is no default target and no default
endpoint.

=opt --suite DIR

C<run>, C<report>: a suite directory, repeatable. For C<report> only the
suites' C<threshold> is taken; without C<--suite> a verdict is judged by its
hard cases alone.

=opt --target NAME

C<run>, required: a Langertha engine -- C<OpenAI> is
L<Langertha::Engine::OpenAI>, a name with C<::> a class name as written -- or
one of the two network-free targets: C<mock-solution> replays every case's
reference solution, C<mock-text> answers text only.

=opt --model M

C<run>: the engine's C<model>.

=opt --url U

C<run>: the engine's C<url>.

=opt --option K=V

C<run>, repeatable: any other constructor argument of the engine. A value that
parses as JSON (a number, C<true>, an object ...) is taken as that, otherwise
as text. C<api_key> is refused -- the command line is visible to every user of
the host.

=opt --label L

C<run>: the target's name in the report and the tables; default the model,
else the engine name.

=opt --variant K=V

=opt --variant NAME:K=V

C<run>, repeatable: the variants of the target, each a name and its
settings, values as for C<--option>. C<K=V> adds to the one unnamed variant,
whose name is its sorted settings (C<max_tokens=4000,temperature=0>);
C<NAME:K=V> adds to the variant C<NAME>, C<NAME:> names one without
settings. Every variant runs every suite; the report has one run per variant
and suite. Without C<--variant> there is one variant, C<default>. The
settings are named and checked (L<Langertha::Holmgang::Target/check_variant>):

=over

=item * C<enable_thinking=on|off> -- sent as
C<chat_template_kwargs.enable_thinking>; only to an OpenAI-compatible engine.

=item * C<reasoning_effort=none|minimal|low|medium|high|xhigh|max> -- only to
an engine that takes it.

=item * C<max_tokens=N> -- 1 to 9999999, beats the case's.

=item * C<temperature=T> -- 0 to 2, beats the case's; only to an engine that
takes it.

=item * C<deadline=S> -- seconds one request may take (above 0, at most
86400); a request that runs out ends the case C<error> with C<timeout:
deadline (S s)>. Needs the engine on an event loop (IO::Async and
Net::Async::HTTP installed). A timeout without data is the engine's
C<user_agent_timeout>: C<--option user_agent_timeout=900>.

=back

Anything else is refused, and so is a setting the engine would drop.

=opt --concurrency N

C<run>: at most N requests open against the target at once, 1 to 64; default
1. Each of the N slots gets its own engine (and connection).

=opt --resume FILE

C<run>: continue the run of an earlier report: every result it holds is taken
over, only the missing ones are played. The report must come from the same
suites (unchanged), target, variants and C<--repeat>; anything else is
refused. C<--report> may name the same file.

=opt --repeat N

C<run>: repetitions per suite, 1 to 100; default the suite's C<repeat>, else 1.

=opt --report FILE

C<run>: write the JSON report there.

=opt --by topic

C<report>: the axis of the evaluation; C<topic> is the only one.

=opt --format F

C<report>: C<text> (default), C<markdown> or C<json>.

=seealso

=over 4

=item * L<Langertha::Holmgang::CLI>

=item * L<Langertha::Holmgang::Report>

=item * L<Langertha::Holmgang::Evaluation>

=back

=cut
